You are helping build "Command Hub": a Discord bot that uses HTTP interactions (no websocket), with an Express backend and a React admin dashboard.

## Tech stack (do not substitute)
- Runtime: Node.js 20+, plain JavaScript with ES modules ("type": "module")
- Backend: Express 4
- Database: Neon Postgres via Prisma ORM (`@prisma/client`). Pooled `DATABASE_URL` (SSL required) for the client; `DIRECT_URL` (non-pooled) for migrations. No raw `pg` driver.
- Discord: `discord-interactions` for Ed25519 verification and response types
- Validation: zod
- Logging: pino with secret redaction
- Auth: bcrypt + jsonwebtoken, JWT stored in an HTTP-only, Secure, SameSite cookie (cookie-parser)
- Security middleware: helmet, express-rate-limit
- Config: dotenv, validated at startup
- Frontend (in /client, built separately): React + Vite + TypeScript + TanStack Query
- Hosting: Render (Express also serves the built React app). Everything must run on free tiers, no credit card.

## Repo layout
/server  Express API, interactions endpoint, retry worker
/client  React dashboard
/docs    api-contract.md (source of truth for API shapes)

## Non-negotiable rules
- Verify the Discord Ed25519 signature on EVERY request to /interactions using the RAW body (express.raw on that route only). Never parse JSON before verifying. Return 401 on failure. Answer type 1 PING with {type:1}.
- Dedup: interactions.id (Discord interaction id) is the primary key. Insert with Prisma `skipDuplicates` (or equivalent unique conflict handling); if no row was inserted, do not re-run side effects.
- Persist the interaction BEFORE any side effect. Side effects (reply follow-up, mirror, AI) are rows in the actions table with status, attempts, last_error, next_retry_at. Failures retry with exponential backoff; nothing is silently dropped.
- Respond within 3 seconds. For slow work return a deferred response (type 5), then PATCH the original response via the interaction webhook.
- Secrets (bot token, public key, webhook URLs, JWT secret, DB URL) come only from env vars, are never logged, never returned by any API. Webhook URLs are write-only; APIs expose only a boolean "mirrorConfigured".
- Prisma only for data access. Do not interpolate user input into `$queryRaw` / `$executeRaw`; use tagged-template parameters if raw SQL is unavoidable. Validate all inputs with zod.
- No business logic in route handlers; use services. Small single-purpose modules.
- Follow docs/api-contract.md exactly.
- Explain any non-obvious decision in a short code comment.
- Build only the step I ask for. Do not add extra features.